            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a clear concrete sealer the same as an invisible one?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              No, and this is the most common point of confusion when shopping for concrete sealer. Many products labeled clear are actually clear acrylic topicals that form a thin surface film, which adds a visible sheen, a slight wet-look gloss, or a small amount of darkening even though the sealer itself has no color. True invisibility requires a penetrating sealer, typically built on silane or siloxane chemistry, that soaks into the concrete pores and reacts below the surface instead of forming a film on top of it.
